{"kind":"request","text":"State refactor S2: separate connection ownership from refresh in the client observer\n\nFrom the implicit-state shortlist in a99e32d9 (audit at e50d9eeb). packages/client/src/observe.ts runs connection renewal, stream pumping, snapshots, cancellation and retries in one closure (observe.ts:63-92). What it may do next depends on combinations of dirty, pending, refreshRunning, streamAlive and generation. The CLI, the Page and the cards all inherit it.\n\nIn one head:\n1. Split the closure into a connection owner (connect, stream, renew, reconnect, stop) and a refresh coordinator (idle, refreshing, coalesced reread).\n2. Give each connection attempt its own resources and its own cleanup, so stopping or renewing one attempt cannot release another's.\n3. Keep the generation check on replies in the refresh coordinator, as the one place that rejects an obsolete reply.\n\nKeep every current guarantee: a refresh requested during a refresh coalesces into one reread; an obsolete reply never replaces a newer snapshot; cancellation during an await leaves no running timer or stream; a late result after timeout or abort is disposed (observe.ts:40); and renewal after an outage keeps its bounds. Use the existing client tests and the callers' tests as witnesses. Add a characterization test only for a guarantee no current test pins, and name it. Keep the exported API unchanged, or list each caller you change. No state-machine framework or library.\n\nStart after S1 (e39e7cef) is in review. Plan 035's M4 keeps its place ahead of both. Run the changed tests while you work and npm run gate once before review. No deploy. Never run rm -rf or rm -f.","body":{"conditions":"One reviewed head on main that splits observe.ts into a connection owner and a refresh coordinator with per-attempt cleanup; every listed guarantee keeps a named witness; exported API unchanged or each caller change listed; changed tests plus one gate before review; checker-approved and landed.","target_head":"bf6ffe617fb1ac6f0e14c39a6f1f93534182bc31","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}